{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589260291,"sessionID":"ses_e2a2563b3ffeIDE7F73WqgBQI8","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5daf564002HVpoFdsnbEtsNt","sessionID":"ses_e2a2563b3ffeIDE7F73WqgBQI8","messageID":"msg_1d5dadaae001fWIxWw8uK2ITTo","type":"tool","id":"call_15f263675b8b4568b044802c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md","offset":108,"limit":20},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md, lines 108-127\n108: - [ ] T022 [P] State the playbook inventory from the tree (`PB`, `PBT`). Test first: in `PBT`, inside the case `keeps the root playbook aligned with the live 50-scenario corpus`, expect `files.filter((file) => /\\/\\d{3}-[^/]*\\.md$/.test(file))` to have length 0, expect `markdown` to contain `The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them` and expect it not to contain `scenario files plus no`. Run `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the new sentence. Then in `PB` replace ``The source root index describes 42 scenarios, but the source category tree contains 41 `NNN-*.md` scenario files plus no `CL-002`.`` with ``The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n109: - [ ] T023 [P] Name the folder scenario results are written to by hand (`PB`, `PBT`). Test first: in `PBT`, add `it('names the folder scenario results are recorded in by hand')`, expecting `markdown` to contain `<!-- MANUAL_PLAYBOOK_RESULT_PERSISTENCE_CONTRACT -->`, `recorded by hand in` and `system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`, and not to contain `renderer-owned`. Run `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and see it fail on `recorded by hand in`. Then in `PB`, keep the marker line and replace the paragraph below it with ``A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome, its reason and its evidence paths are recorded by hand in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`. The first recorded run creates that folder, because the wrapper that once wrote these records was retired and no renderer writes them now.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n110: - [ ] T024 [P] Describe the playbook test as the inventory test it is (`TR`). Replace the row ``| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures. |`` with ``| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Checks the playbook inventory: the root playbook lists every scenario file in the category tree once, and its persistence note names the folder results are recorded in. |`` Verify: `rg -c \"Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures\" $TR` prints nothing and `rg -c \"Checks the playbook inventory\" $TR` prints 1.\n111: \n112: ### Wave 1, lane WG6: OpenCode plugin residue and field tests\n113: - [ ] T025 [P] Correct the bounding option's jsdoc (`PJ`). Replace ` * @param {boolean} [rawOptions.boundedCompiledRouteSummary] - Bound long compiled-route target lists` with ` * @param {boolean} [rawOptions.boundedCompiledRouteSummary] - Reported as the bounded_compiled_route_summary status field. The brief carries no compiled-route line, so it bounds nothing`. Verify: `rg -c \"Bound long compiled-route target lists\" $PJ` prints nothing, `node --check $PJ` exits 0 and `VP` reports `fail 0`.\n114: - [ ] T026 [P] Remove the route summary nothing reads (`PJ`). Delete the function `compiledRouteSummary(data)` with the comment block above it, the line `const routeSummary = compiledRouteSummary(data);` and the line `...(routeSummary ? { compiledRouteSummary: routeSummary } : {}),` in the returned metadata. Verify: `rg -c \"compiledRouteSummary\" $PJ` prints nothing, `node --check $PJ` exits 0 and `VP` reports `fail 0`.\n115: - [ ] T027 [P] Test the command fields on the plugin path (`PJT`). Add `test('renders the command, its policy and its owner from the advisor row')`, which saves and deletes `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD`, builds the plugin with `makePlugin({ spawnOverride: spawnSequence([fakeChild({ stdout: cliEnvelope({ recommendations: [{ skillId: 'sk-doc', score: 0.9, confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }] }) })]) })`, awaits `runPrompt(hooks)`, restores the variable in a `finally` and asserts that `output.system[0]` contains `sk-doc → /create:agent (start)`. This case passes today and fails when the plugin drops a field. Verify: `VP` reports `fail 0` and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node TSX $PL/probe-plugin-fields.mts` prints `plugin test asserts a command label: true`.\n116: - [ ] T028 [P] Test the command fields on the fallback path (`ENV`). Add `it('keeps the command, its policy and its owner from a CLI row')`, which calls `resultFromCliData` with `data: { freshness: 'live', recommendations: [{ skillId: 'sk-doc', confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }] }` and the `options`, `startedAt` and `now` the existing cases pass, expects `result.recommendations[0]` to match `{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }` and expects the first line of `renderAdvisorBrief(result)` to contain `sk-doc → /create:agent (start)`. This case passes today and fails when a field is dropped. Verify: `VX tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n117: \n118: ### Wave 1, lane WG7: subprocess busy scan and catalog anchors\n119: - [ ] T029 [P] See a busy marker past the stderr cap (`SUB`, `SUBT`). Test first: in `SUBT`, rename the case `stops reading stderr at the cap, so a busy marker past it is not seen` to `retries once on a busy marker written after the cap`, expect `errorCode` `SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED` and `retriesAttempted` 1, and replace the comment above it with one saying the cap bounds what is kept, not what is scanned. Add `it('retries once on a busy marker split across two writes after the cap')`, whose child writes `'e'.repeat(1024 * 1024)`, then `'\\ndatabase is '`, waits 20 ms, writes `'locked\\n'` and exits 1, expecting the same two values, so neither write alone holds the marker. Run `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and see both report `NON_ZERO_EXIT`. Then in `SUB` add `readonly sawBusy: boolean;` to `SpawnAttemptResult`, keep a `busyCarry` string and a `sawBusy` flag in `runSpawnAttempt`, and in the stderr `data` handler, before `capOutput`, test `SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN` against `busyCarry + chunk` until it matches, keeping the last 64 characters as the next `busyCarry`. Report `sawBusy` in every `resolve` call and read the retry decision as `attemptResult.sawBusy || SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN.test(attemptResult.stderr)`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/legacy/advisor-subprocess.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `node TSX $PL/probe-busy-cap.mts` prints `marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1`.\n120: - [ ] T030 [P] Cite the catalog's schema and handler anchors by name (`ARM`). Replace `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308` `` with ``the `compiledRoute` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310` `` with ``the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634` `` with ``the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` ``, and each of `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287` `` and `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290` `` with ``the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``. Leave the citations of `lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, `tools/advisor-recommend.ts` and `skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts`. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts:[0-9]\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendationSchema\" $ARM` prints 3, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendInputSchema\" $ARM` prints 2 and `bash $PL/probe-catalog-lines.sh` prints no `advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and no `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` line.\n121: \n122: ### Wave 1, lane WG8: doctor embed and setup contracts\n123: - [ ] T031 [P] Give a failed restore its own exit-3 outcome (`DAE`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow reads a failed restore as a partly written tree')`, which takes the one line of `EMBED_YAML` that contains `Exit 3 means` and asserts it matches `/ERROR: the restore failed/`, `/quote both ERROR lines/` and `/takes precedence over the restored: outcome/`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on the first pattern. Then in `DAE`, inside the same quoted string that starts `Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup.`, append `When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0 and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `workflow names the restore failure: 1`.\n124: - [ ] T032 [P] Name the backup folder by the plan digest (`DAE`, `RTS`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow and route name the backup folder the engine makes')`, asserting that `EMBED_YAML` and `routeFor('embed').gate3_location` each contain `doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/` and not `<timestamp>`, and that the route text contains `temporary directory`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on `<timestamp>`. Then in `DAE` replace `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/` with `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/`, and in `RTS`, inside the embed route's `gate3_location`, replace `taken to the plan's backup folder under .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ before the first byte` with `taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes`.\n125: - [ ] T033 [P] Give the setup router the workflow's reason for absent hook health (`DSM`, `DSCT`). Test first: in `DSCT`, inside `test('the setup workflow and router both name the unrecorded hook health state'`, add `assert.match(SETUP_ROUTER, /because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet/)` and `assert.doesNotMatch(SETUP_ROUTER, /SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/)`. Run `NT $DSCT` and see it fail on the first assertion. Then in `DSM` replace ``When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.`` with `When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 0` and `RV` and `SRM` exit 0.\n126: \n127: ### Wave 1, lane WG9: doctor check scripts\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 128]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md, lines 108-127\n108: - [ ] T022 [P] State the playbook inventory from the tree (`PB`, `PBT`). Test first: in `PBT`, inside the case `keeps the root playbook aligned with the live 50-scenario corpus`, expect `files.filter((file) => /\\/\\d{3}-[^/]*\\.md$/.test(file))` to have length 0, expect `markdown` to contain `The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them` and expect it not to contain `scenario files plus no`. Run `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the new sentence. Then in `PB` replace ``The source root index describes 42 scenarios, but the source category tree contains 41 `NNN-*.md` scenario files plus no `CL-002`.`` with ``The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n109: - [ ] T023 [P] Name the folder scenario results are written to by hand (`PB`, `PBT`). Test first: in `PBT`, add `it('names the folder scenario results are recorded in by hand')`, expecting `markdown` to contain `<!-- MANUAL_PLAYBOOK_RESULT_PERSISTENCE_CONTRACT -->`, `recorded by hand in` and `system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`, and not to contain `renderer-owned`. Run `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and see it fail on `recorded by hand in`. Then in `PB`, keep the marker line and replace the paragraph below it with ``A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome, its reason and its evidence paths are recorded by hand in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`. The first recorded run creates that folder, because the wrapper that once wrote these records was retired and no renderer writes them now.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n110: - [ ] T024 [P] Describe the playbook test as the inventory test it is (`TR`). Replace the row ``| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures. |`` with ``| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Checks the playbook inventory: the root playbook lists every scenario file in the category tree once, and its persistence note names the folder results are recorded in. |`` Verify: `rg -c \"Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures\" $TR` prints nothing and `rg -c \"Checks the playbook inventory\" $TR` prints 1.\n111: \n112: ### Wave 1, lane WG6: OpenCode plugin residue and field tests\n113: - [ ] T025 [P] Correct the bounding option's jsdoc (`PJ`). Replace ` * @param {boolean} [rawOptions.boundedCompiledRouteSummary] - Bound long compiled-route target lists` with ` * @param {boolean} [rawOptions.boundedCompiledRouteSummary] - Reported as the bounded_compiled_route_summary status field. The brief carries no compiled-route line, so it bounds nothing`. Verify: `rg -c \"Bound long compiled-route target lists\" $PJ` prints nothing, `node --check $PJ` exits 0 and `VP` reports `fail 0`.\n114: - [ ] T026 [P] Remove the route summary nothing reads (`PJ`). Delete the function `compiledRouteSummary(data)` with the comment block above it, the line `const routeSummary = compiledRouteSummary(data);` and the line `...(routeSummary ? { compiledRouteSummary: routeSummary } : {}),` in the returned metadata. Verify: `rg -c \"compiledRouteSummary\" $PJ` prints nothing, `node --check $PJ` exits 0 and `VP` reports `fail 0`.\n115: - [ ] T027 [P] Test the command fields on the plugin path (`PJT`). Add `test('renders the command, its policy and its owner from the advisor row')`, which saves and deletes `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD`, builds the plugin with `makePlugin({ spawnOverride: spawnSequence([fakeChild({ stdout: cliEnvelope({ recommendations: [{ skillId: 'sk-doc', score: 0.9, confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }] }) })]) })`, awaits `runPrompt(hooks)`, restores the variable in a `finally` and asserts that `output.system[0]` contains `sk-doc → /create:agent (start)`. This case passes today and fails when the plugin drops a field. Verify: `VP` reports `fail 0` and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node TSX $PL/probe-plugin-fields.mts` prints `plugin test asserts a command label: true`.\n116: - [ ] T028 [P] Test the command fields on the fallback path (`ENV`). Add `it('keeps the command, its policy and its owner from a CLI row')`, which calls `resultFromCliData` with `data: { freshness: 'live', recommendations: [{ skillId: 'sk-doc', confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }] }` and the `options`, `startedAt` and `now` the existing cases pass, expects `result.recommendations[0]` to match `{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }` and expects the first line of `renderAdvisorBrief(result)` to contain `sk-doc → /create:agent (start)`. This case passes today and fails when a field is dropped. Verify: `VX tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n117: \n118: ### Wave 1, lane WG7: subprocess busy scan and catalog anchors\n119: - [ ] T029 [P] See a busy marker past the stderr cap (`SUB`, `SUBT`). Test first: in `SUBT`, rename the case `stops reading stderr at the cap, so a busy marker past it is not seen` to `retries once on a busy marker written after the cap`, expect `errorCode` `SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED` and `retriesAttempted` 1, and replace the comment above it with one saying the cap bounds what is kept, not what is scanned. Add `it('retries once on a busy marker split across two writes after the cap')`, whose child writes `'e'.repeat(1024 * 1024)`, then `'\\ndatabase is '`, waits 20 ms, writes `'locked\\n'` and exits 1, expecting the same two values, so neither write alone holds the marker. Run `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and see both report `NON_ZERO_EXIT`. Then in `SUB` add `readonly sawBusy: boolean;` to `SpawnAttemptResult`, keep a `busyCarry` string and a `sawBusy` flag in `runSpawnAttempt`, and in the stderr `data` handler, before `capOutput`, test `SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN` against `busyCarry + chunk` until it matches, keeping the last 64 characters as the next `busyCarry`. Report `sawBusy` in every `resolve` call and read the retry decision as `attemptResult.sawBusy || SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN.test(attemptResult.stderr)`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/legacy/advisor-subprocess.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `node TSX $PL/probe-busy-cap.mts` prints `marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1`.\n120: - [ ] T030 [P] Cite the catalog's schema and handler anchors by name (`ARM`). Replace `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308` `` with ``the `compiledRoute` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310` `` with ``the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634` `` with ``the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` ``, and each of `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287` `` and `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290` `` with ``the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``. Leave the citations of `lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, `tools/advisor-recommend.ts` and `skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts`. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts:[0-9]\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendationSchema\" $ARM` prints 3, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendInputSchema\" $ARM` prints 2 and `bash $PL/probe-catalog-lines.sh` prints no `advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and no `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` line.\n121: \n122: ### Wave 1, lane WG8: doctor embed and setup contracts\n123: - [ ] T031 [P] Give a failed restore its own exit-3 outcome (`DAE`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow reads a failed restore as a partly written tree')`, which takes the one line of `EMBED_YAML` that contains `Exit 3 means` and asserts it matches `/ERROR: the restore failed/`, `/quote both ERROR lines/` and `/takes precedence over the restored: outcome/`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on the first pattern. Then in `DAE`, inside the same quoted string that starts `Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup.`, append `When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0 and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `workflow names the restore failure: 1`.\n124: - [ ] T032 [P] Name the backup folder by the plan digest (`DAE`, `RTS`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow and route name the backup folder the engine makes')`, asserting that `EMBED_YAML` and `routeFor('embed').gate3_location` each contain `doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/` and not `<timestamp>`, and that the route text contains `temporary directory`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on `<timestamp>`. Then in `DAE` replace `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/` with `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/`, and in `RTS`, inside the embed route's `gate3_location`, replace `taken to the plan's backup folder under .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ before the first byte` with `taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes`.\n125: - [ ] T033 [P] Give the setup router the workflow's reason for absent hook health (`DSM`, `DSCT`). Test first: in `DSCT`, inside `test('the setup workflow and router both name the unrecorded hook health state'`, add `assert.match(SETUP_ROUTER, /because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet/)` and `assert.doesNotMatch(SETUP_ROUTER, /SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/)`. Run `NT $DSCT` and see it fail on the first assertion. Then in `DSM` replace ``When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.`` with `When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 0` and `RV` and `SRM` exit 0.\n126: \n127: ### Wave 1, lane WG9: doctor check scripts\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 128]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md\",\"offset\":108,\"limit\":20}"},"time":{"start":1794589259108,"end":1794589260291}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589260374,"sessionID":"ses_e2a2563b3ffeIDE7F73WqgBQI8","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5daf878001lKU3gbgUb35TN0","sessionID":"ses_e2a2563b3ffeIDE7F73WqgBQI8","messageID":"msg_1d5dadaae001fWIxWw8uK2ITTo","type":"tool","id":"call_fab22dc419914fceb46a53cb","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts, lines 1-409\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Skill Advisor Subprocess Runner\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\n10: import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { join } from 'node:path';\n12: import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks';\n13: \n14: import { isRecord } from './utils/json-guard.js';\n15: \n16: import type { ChildProcess } from 'node:child_process';\n17: import type { AdvisorThresholds } from './prompt-cache.js';\n18: import { SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPAT_CONTRACT, resolvedConfidenceThreshold, resolvedUncertaintyThreshold } from './compat/contract.js';\n19: \n20: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: // 2. TYPE DEFINITIONS\n22: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: \n24: /**\n25:  * Compact summary of a compiled routing decision, small enough to cross the\n26:  * brief boundary without carrying the full internal decision object. The served\n27:  * outcome is one of route/clarify/defer/reject; the fingerprint is the manifest\n28:  * serving-state hash used to invalidate a stale cached brief.\n29:  */\n30: export interface CompiledRouteSummary {\n31:   readonly outcome: string;\n32:   readonly hubId: string | null;\n33:   readonly targets: readonly string[];\n34:   readonly servingAuthority: string;\n35:   readonly fingerprint: string | null;\n36:   readonly generation: number | null;\n37: }\n38: \n39: export interface AdvisorRecommendation {\n40:   readonly skill: string;\n41:   readonly kind?: string;\n42:   readonly command?: string;\n43:   readonly policy?: string;\n44:   readonly ownerSkillId?: string;\n45:   // True when a hub held back its command because the prompt names no single mode.\n46:   readonly needsMode?: boolean;\n47:   readonly confidence: number;\n48:   readonly uncertainty: number;\n49:   readonly passes_threshold?: boolean;\n50:   readonly reason?: string;\n51:   // Additive: the compiled decision summary when a hub is compiled-serving. This\n52:   // path parses the Python advisor stdout, which does not emit it today, but the\n53:   // interface must not structurally drop it so a compiled decision reaching this\n54:   // brief path survives instead of being silently stripped.\n55:   readonly compiledRouteSummary?: CompiledRouteSummary;\n56: }\n57: \n58: export type AdvisorSubprocessErrorCode =\n59:   | 'PYTHON_MISSING'\n60:   | 'SCRIPT_MISSING'\n61:   | 'SIGNAL_KILLED'\n62:   | 'TIMEOUT'\n63:   | 'JSON_PARSE_FAILED'\n64:   | 'INVALID_JSON_SHAPE'\n65:   | 'NON_ZERO_EXIT'\n66:   | 'SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED'\n67:   | 'SPAWN_ERROR';\n68: \n69: export interface AdvisorSubprocessResult {\n70:   readonly ok: boolean;\n71:   readonly recommendations: AdvisorRecommendation[];\n72:   readonly errorCode: AdvisorSubprocessErrorCode | null;\n73:   readonly exitCode: number | null;\n74:   readonly signal: NodeJS.Signals | null;\n75:   readonly stderr: string | null;\n76:   readonly durationMs: number;\n77:   readonly retriesAttempted: number;\n78: }\n79: \n80: export interface AdvisorSubprocessOptions {\n81:   readonly workspaceRoot: string;\n82:   readonly timeoutMs?: number;\n83:   readonly thresholdConfig?: AdvisorThresholds;\n84:   readonly pythonBin?: string;\n85:   readonly scriptPath?: string;\n86:   readonly retryJitterMs?: () => number;\n87: }\n88: \n89: interface SpawnAttemptResult {\n90:   readonly ok: boolean;\n91:   readonly stdout: string;\n92:   readonly stderr: string;\n93:   readonly exitCode: number | null;\n94:   readonly signal: NodeJS.Signals | null;\n95:   readonly errorCode: AdvisorSubprocessErrorCode | null;\n96:   readonly durationMs: number;\n97: }\n98: \n99: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n100: // 3. CONSTANTS\n101: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n102: \n103: const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000;\n104: const MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024;\n105: const SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN = /\\bSQLITE_BUSY\\b|database is locked/i;\n106: \n107: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n108: // 4. HELPERS\n109: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n110: \n111: function parsePositiveInt(value: string | undefined, fallback: number): number {\n112:   if (typeof value !== 'string' || value.trim().length === 0) {\n113:     return fallback;\n114:   }\n115:   const parsed = Number.parseInt(value, 10);\n116:   return Number.isFinite(parsed) && parsed > 0 ? parsed : fallback;\n117: }\n118: \n119: function defaultTimeoutMs(): number {\n120:   return parsePositiveInt(process.env.SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS);\n121: }\n122: \n123: function thresholdArgs(thresholdConfig: AdvisorThresholds | undefined): string[] {\n124:   const confidenceThreshold = String(thresholdConfig?.confidenceThreshold ?? resolvedConfidenceThreshold());\n125:   const uncertaintyThreshold = String(thresholdConfig?.uncertaintyThreshold ?? resolvedUncertaintyThreshold());\n126:   const args = ['--threshold', confidenceThreshold, '--uncertainty', uncertaintyThreshold];\n127:   if (thresholdConfig?.confidenceOnly) {\n128:     args.push('--confidence-only');\n129:   }\n130:   if (thresholdConfig?.showRejections) {\n131:     args.push('--show-rejections');\n132:   }\n133:   return args;\n134: }\n135: \n136: function sanitizeStderr(stderr: string): string | null {\n137:   const compact = stderr.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n138:   if (!compact) {\n139:     return null;\n140:   }\n141:   return compact.slice(0, 240);\n142: }\n143: \n144: // Only the timeout bounded the child's output before, so a runaway child could\n145: // hold the hook's memory until it was killed. Both streams stop growing at the\n146: // cap instead.\n147: function capOutput(current: string, chunk: string): string {\n148:   if (current.length >= MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS) {\n149:     return current;\n150:   }\n151:   return (current + chunk).slice(0, MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS);\n152: }\n153: \n154: function coerceCompiledRouteSummary(value: unknown): CompiledRouteSummary | undefined {\n155:   if (!isRecord(value)) return undefined;\n156:   if (typeof value.outcome !== 'string' || value.outcome.length === 0) return undefined;\n157:   const targets = Array.isArray(value.targets)\n158:     ? value.targets.filter((target): target is string => typeof target === 'string')\n159:     : [];\n160:   return {\n161:     outcome: value.outcome,\n162:     hubId: typeof value.hubId === 'string' ? value.hubId : null,\n163:     targets,\n164:     servingAuthority: typeof value.servingAuthority === 'string' ? value.servingAuthority : 'compiled',\n165:     fingerprint: typeof value.fingerprint === 'string' ? value.fingerprint : null,\n166:     generation: typeof value.generation === 'number' ? value.generation : null,\n167:   };\n168: }\n169: \n170: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n171: // 5. CORE LOGIC\n172: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n173: \n174: function parseRecommendations(stdout: string): AdvisorRecommendation[] {\n175:   const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(stdout);\n176:   if (!Array.isArray(parsed)) {\n177:     throw new Error(`advisor stdout: expected JSON array; actual ${typeof parsed}.`);\n178:   }\n179:   return parsed.map((item, index) => {\n180:     const path = `advisor stdout[${index}]`;\n181:     if (!isRecord(item)) {\n182:       throw new Error(`${path}: expected object recommendation; actual ${typeof item}.`);\n183:     }\n184:     if (typeof item.skill !== 'string' || item.skill.trim().length === 0) {\n185:       throw new Error(`${path}.skill: expected non-empty string; actual ${typeof item.skill}.`);\n186:     }\n187:     if (typeof item.confidence !== 'number' || Number.isNaN(item.confidence)) {\n188:       throw new Error(`${path}.confidence: expected finite number; actual ${typeof item.confidence}.`);\n189:     }\n190:     if (typeof item.uncertainty !== 'number' || Number.isNaN(item.uncertainty)) {\n191:       throw new Error(`${path}.uncertainty: expected finite number; actual ${typeof item.uncertainty}.`);\n192:     }\n193:     const compiledRouteSummary = coerceCompiledRouteSummary(item.compiledRouteSummary);\n194:     return {\n195:       skill: item.skill,\n196:       ...(typeof item.kind === 'string' ? { kind: item.kind } : {}),\n197:       confidence: item.confidence,\n198:       uncertainty: item.uncertainty,\n199:       ...(typeof item.passes_threshold === 'boolean' ? { passes_threshold: item.passes_threshold } : {}),\n200:       ...(typeof item.reason === 'string' ? { reason: item.reason } : {}),\n201:       ...(compiledRouteSummary ? { compiledRouteSummary } : {}),\n202:     };\n203:   });\n204: }\n205: \n206: function runSpawnAttempt(args: {\n207:   command: string;\n208:   commandArgs: readonly string[];\n209:   prompt: string;\n210:   cwd: string;\n211:   timeoutMs: number;\n212: }): Promise<SpawnAttemptResult> {\n213:   const startedAt = performance.now();\n214:   return new Promise((resolve) => {\n215:     let stdout = '';\n216:     let stderr = '';\n217:     let settled = false;\n218:     let timedOut = false;\n219:     let child: ChildProcess;\n220: \n221:     try {\n222:       child = spawn(args.command, args.commandArgs, {\n223:         cwd: args.cwd,\n224:         env: process.env,\n225:         stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n226:       });\n227:     } catch (error: unknown) {\n228:       resolve({\n229:         ok: false,\n230:         stdout,\n231:         stderr: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'spawn failed',\n232:         exitCode: null,\n233:         signal: null,\n234:         errorCode: 'SPAWN_ERROR',\n235:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n236:       });\n237:       return;\n238:     }\n239: \n240:     child.stdin?.write(args.prompt);\n241:     child.stdin?.end();\n242:     const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n243:       timedOut = true;\n244:       child.kill('SIGKILL');\n245:     }, args.timeoutMs);\n246: \n247:     child.stdout?.setEncoding('utf8');\n248:     child.stderr?.setEncoding('utf8');\n249:     child.stdout?.on('data', (chunk: string) => {\n250:       stdout = capOutput(stdout, chunk);\n251:     });\n252:     child.stderr?.on('data', (chunk: string) => {\n253:       stderr = capOutput(stderr, chunk);\n254:     });\n255:     child.on('error', (error: NodeJS.ErrnoException) => {\n256:       if (settled) {\n257:         return;\n258:       }\n259:       settled = true;\n260:       clearTimeout(timer);\n261:       resolve({\n262:         ok: false,\n263:         stdout,\n264:         stderr: error.message,\n265:         exitCode: null,\n266:         signal: null,\n267:         errorCode: error.code === 'ENOENT' ? 'PYTHON_MISSING' : 'SPAWN_ERROR',\n268:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n269:       });\n270:     });\n271:     child.on('close', (exitCode: number | null, signal: NodeJS.Signals | null) => {\n272:       if (settled) {\n273:         return;\n274:       }\n275:       settled = true;\n276:       clearTimeout(timer);\n277:       resolve({\n278:         ok: exitCode === 0 && signal === null && !timedOut,\n279:         stdout,\n280:         stderr,\n281:         exitCode,\n282:         signal,\n283:         errorCode: timedOut || performance.now() - startedAt >= args.timeoutMs\n284:           ? 'TIMEOUT'\n285:           : signal === 'SIGKILL'\n286:             ? 'SIGNAL_KILLED'\n287:             : null,\n288:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n289:       });\n290:     });\n291:   });\n292: }\n293: \n294: async function delay(ms: number): Promise<void> {\n295:   await new Promise((resolve) => {\n296:     setTimeout(resolve, ms);\n297:   });\n298: }\n299: \n300: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n301: // 6. EXPORTS\n302: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n303: \n304: /** Run the Python skill advisor with prompt input carried over stdin. */\n305: export async function runAdvisorSubprocess(\n306:   prompt: string,\n307:   options: AdvisorSubprocessOptions,\n308: ): Promise<AdvisorSubprocessResult> {\n309:   const timeoutMs = options.timeoutMs ?? defaultTimeoutMs();\n310:   const scriptPath = options.scriptPath\n311:     ?? join(\n312:       options.workspaceRoot,\n313:       '.skilled',\n314:       'skills',\n315:       'system-skill-advisor',\n316:       'runtime',\n317:       'scripts',\n318:       'skill_advisor.py',\n319:     );\n320:   const startedAt = performance.now();\n321:   let retriesAttempted = 0;\n322: \n323:   if (!existsSync(scriptPath)) {\n324:     return {\n325:       ok: false,\n326:       recommendations: [],\n327:       errorCode: 'SCRIPT_MISSING',\n328:       exitCode: null,\n329:       signal: null,\n330:       stderr: null,\n331:       durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n332:       retriesAttempted,\n333:     };\n334:   }\n335: \n336:   const commandArgs = [\n337:     scriptPath,\n338:     ...thresholdArgs(options.thresholdConfig),\n339:     '--stdin',\n340:   ];\n341:   const command = options.pythonBin ?? 'python3';\n342: \n343:   for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 2; attempt += 1) {\n344:     const elapsedMs = performance.now() - startedAt;\n345:     const remainingMs = Math.max(0, timeoutMs - elapsedMs);\n346:     const attemptResult = await runSpawnAttempt({\n347:       command,\n348:       commandArgs,\n349:       prompt,\n350:       cwd: options.workspaceRoot,\n351:       timeoutMs: Math.max(1, remainingMs),\n352:     });\n353: \n354:     if (!attemptResult.ok) {\n355:       const busy = SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN.test(attemptResult.stderr);\n356:       const budgetRemaining = timeoutMs - (performance.now() - startedAt);\n357:       if (busy && attempt === 0 && budgetRemaining >= 500) {\n358:         retriesAttempted = 1;\n359:         await delay(options.retryJitterMs?.() ?? 75 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 51));\n360:         continue;\n361:       }\n362:       return {\n363:         ok: false,\n364:         recommendations: [],\n365:         errorCode: busy ? 'SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED' : attemptResult.errorCode ?? 'NON_ZERO_EXIT',\n366:         exitCode: attemptResult.exitCode,\n367:         signal: attemptResult.signal,\n368:         stderr: sanitizeStderr(attemptResult.stderr),\n369:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n370:         retriesAttempted,\n371:       };\n372:     }\n373: \n374:     try {\n375:       return {\n376:         ok: true,\n377:         recommendations: parseRecommendations(attemptResult.stdout),\n378:         errorCode: null,\n379:         exitCode: attemptResult.exitCode,\n380:         signal: attemptResult.signal,\n381:         stderr: sanitizeStderr(attemptResult.stderr),\n382:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n383:         retriesAttempted,\n384:       };\n385:     } catch (error: unknown) {\n386:       return {\n387:         ok: false,\n388:         recommendations: [],\n389:         errorCode: error instanceof SyntaxError ? 'JSON_PARSE_FAILED' : 'INVALID_JSON_SHAPE',\n390:         exitCode: attemptResult.exitCode,\n391:         signal: attemptResult.signal,\n392:         stderr: null,\n393:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n394:         retriesAttempted,\n395:       };\n396:     }\n397:   }\n398: \n399:   return {\n400:     ok: false,\n401:     recommendations: [],\n402:     errorCode: 'SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED',\n403:     exitCode: null,\n404:     signal: null,\n405:     stderr: null,\n406:     durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n407:     retriesAttempted,\n408:   };\n409: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts, lines 1-409\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Skill Advisor Subprocess Runner\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\n10: import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { join } from 'node:path';\n12: import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks';\n13: \n14: import { isRecord } from './utils/json-guard.js';\n15: \n16: import type { ChildProcess } from 'node:child_process';\n17: import type { AdvisorThresholds } from './prompt-cache.js';\n18: import { SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPAT_CONTRACT, resolvedConfidenceThreshold, resolvedUncertaintyThreshold } from './compat/contract.js';\n19: \n20: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: // 2. TYPE DEFINITIONS\n22: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: \n24: /**\n25:  * Compact summary of a compiled routing decision, small enough to cross the\n26:  * brief boundary without carrying the full internal decision object. The served\n27:  * outcome is one of route/clarify/defer/reject; the fingerprint is the manifest\n28:  * serving-state hash used to invalidate a stale cached brief.\n29:  */\n30: export interface CompiledRouteSummary {\n31:   readonly outcome: string;\n32:   readonly hubId: string | null;\n33:   readonly targets: readonly string[];\n34:   readonly servingAuthority: string;\n35:   readonly fingerprint: string | null;\n36:   readonly generation: number | null;\n37: }\n38: \n39: export interface AdvisorRecommendation {\n40:   readonly skill: string;\n41:   readonly kind?: string;\n42:   readonly command?: string;\n43:   readonly policy?: string;\n44:   readonly ownerSkillId?: string;\n45:   // True when a hub held back its command because the prompt names no single mode.\n46:   readonly needsMode?: boolean;\n47:   readonly confidence: number;\n48:   readonly uncertainty: number;\n49:   readonly passes_threshold?: boolean;\n50:   readonly reason?: string;\n51:   // Additive: the compiled decision summary when a hub is compiled-serving. This\n52:   // path parses the Python advisor stdout, which does not emit it today, but the\n53:   // interface must not structurally drop it so a compiled decision reaching this\n54:   // brief path survives instead of being silently stripped.\n55:   readonly compiledRouteSummary?: CompiledRouteSummary;\n56: }\n57: \n58: export type AdvisorSubprocessErrorCode =\n59:   | 'PYTHON_MISSING'\n60:   | 'SCRIPT_MISSING'\n61:   | 'SIGNAL_KILLED'\n62:   | 'TIMEOUT'\n63:   | 'JSON_PARSE_FAILED'\n64:   | 'INVALID_JSON_SHAPE'\n65:   | 'NON_ZERO_EXIT'\n66:   | 'SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED'\n67:   | 'SPAWN_ERROR';\n68: \n69: export interface AdvisorSubprocessResult {\n70:   readonly ok: boolean;\n71:   readonly recommendations: AdvisorRecommendation[];\n72:   readonly errorCode: AdvisorSubprocessErrorCode | null;\n73:   readonly exitCode: number | null;\n74:   readonly signal: NodeJS.Signals | null;\n75:   readonly stderr: string | null;\n76:   readonly durationMs: number;\n77:   readonly retriesAttempted: number;\n78: }\n79: \n80: export interface AdvisorSubprocessOptions {\n81:   readonly workspaceRoot: string;\n82:   readonly timeoutMs?: number;\n83:   readonly thresholdConfig?: AdvisorThresholds;\n84:   readonly pythonBin?: string;\n85:   readonly scriptPath?: string;\n86:   readonly retryJitterMs?: () => number;\n87: }\n88: \n89: interface SpawnAttemptResult {\n90:   readonly ok: boolean;\n91:   readonly stdout: string;\n92:   readonly stderr: string;\n93:   readonly exitCode: number | null;\n94:   readonly signal: NodeJS.Signals | null;\n95:   readonly errorCode: AdvisorSubprocessErrorCode | null;\n96:   readonly durationMs: number;\n97: }\n98: \n99: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n100: // 3. CONSTANTS\n101: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n102: \n103: const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000;\n104: const MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024;\n105: const SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN = /\\bSQLITE_BUSY\\b|database is locked/i;\n106: \n107: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n108: // 4. HELPERS\n109: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n110: \n111: function parsePositiveInt(value: string | undefined, fallback: number): number {\n112:   if (typeof value !== 'string' || value.trim().length === 0) {\n113:     return fallback;\n114:   }\n115:   const parsed = Number.parseInt(value, 10);\n116:   return Number.isFinite(parsed) && parsed > 0 ? parsed : fallback;\n117: }\n118: \n119: function defaultTimeoutMs(): number {\n120:   return parsePositiveInt(process.env.SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS);\n121: }\n122: \n123: function thresholdArgs(thresholdConfig: AdvisorThresholds | undefined): string[] {\n124:   const confidenceThreshold = String(thresholdConfig?.confidenceThreshold ?? resolvedConfidenceThreshold());\n125:   const uncertaintyThreshold = String(thresholdConfig?.uncertaintyThreshold ?? resolvedUncertaintyThreshold());\n126:   const args = ['--threshold', confidenceThreshold, '--uncertainty', uncertaintyThreshold];\n127:   if (thresholdConfig?.confidenceOnly) {\n128:     args.push('--confidence-only');\n129:   }\n130:   if (thresholdConfig?.showRejections) {\n131:     args.push('--show-rejections');\n132:   }\n133:   return args;\n134: }\n135: \n136: function sanitizeStderr(stderr: string): string | null {\n137:   const compact = stderr.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n138:   if (!compact) {\n139:     return null;\n140:   }\n141:   return compact.slice(0, 240);\n142: }\n143: \n144: // Only the timeout bounded the child's output before, so a runaway child could\n145: // hold the hook's memory until it was killed. Both streams stop growing at the\n146: // cap instead.\n147: function capOutput(current: string, chunk: string): string {\n148:   if (current.length >= MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS) {\n149:     return current;\n150:   }\n151:   return (current + chunk).slice(0, MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS);\n152: }\n153: \n154: function coerceCompiledRouteSummary(value: unknown): CompiledRouteSummary | undefined {\n155:   if (!isRecord(value)) return undefined;\n156:   if (typeof value.outcome !== 'string' || value.outcome.length === 0) return undefined;\n157:   const targets = Array.isArray(value.targets)\n158:     ? value.targets.filter((target): target is string => typeof target === 'string')\n159:     : [];\n160:   return {\n161:     outcome: value.outcome,\n162:     hubId: typeof value.hubId === 'string' ? value.hubId : null,\n163:     targets,\n164:     servingAuthority: typeof value.servingAuthority === 'string' ? value.servingAuthority : 'compiled',\n165:     fingerprint: typeof value.fingerprint === 'string' ? value.fingerprint : null,\n166:     generation: typeof value.generation === 'number' ? value.generation : null,\n167:   };\n168: }\n169: \n170: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n171: // 5. CORE LOGIC\n172: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n173: \n174: function parseRecommendations(stdout: string): AdvisorRecommendation[] {\n175:   const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(stdout);\n176:   if (!Array.isArray(parsed)) {\n177:     throw new Error(`advisor stdout: expected JSON array; actual ${typeof parsed}.`);\n178:   }\n179:   return parsed.map((item, index) => {\n180:     const path = `advisor stdout[${index}]`;\n181:     if (!isRecord(item)) {\n182:       throw new Error(`${path}: expected object recommendation; actual ${typeof item}.`);\n183:     }\n184:     if (typeof item.skill !== 'string' || item.skill.trim().length === 0) {\n185:       throw new Error(`${path}.skill: expected non-empty string; actual ${typeof item.skill}.`);\n186:     }\n187:     if (typeof item.confidence !== 'number' || Number.isNaN(item.confidence)) {\n188:       throw new Error(`${path}.confidence: expected finite number; actual ${typeof item.confidence}.`);\n189:     }\n190:     if (typeof item.uncertainty !== 'number' || Number.isNaN(item.uncertainty)) {\n191:       throw new Error(`${path}.uncertainty: expected finite number; actual ${typeof item.uncertainty}.`);\n192:     }\n193:     const compiledRouteSummary = coerceCompiledRouteSummary(item.compiledRouteSummary);\n194:     return {\n195:       skill: item.skill,\n196:       ...(typeof item.kind === 'string' ? { kind: item.kind } : {}),\n197:       confidence: item.confidence,\n198:       uncertainty: item.uncertainty,\n199:       ...(typeof item.passes_threshold === 'boolean' ? { passes_threshold: item.passes_threshold } : {}),\n200:       ...(typeof item.reason === 'string' ? { reason: item.reason } : {}),\n201:       ...(compiledRouteSummary ? { compiledRouteSummary } : {}),\n202:     };\n203:   });\n204: }\n205: \n206: function runSpawnAttempt(args: {\n207:   command: string;\n208:   commandArgs: readonly string[];\n209:   prompt: string;\n210:   cwd: string;\n211:   timeoutMs: number;\n212: }): Promise<SpawnAttemptResult> {\n213:   const startedAt = performance.now();\n214:   return new Promise((resolve) => {\n215:     let stdout = '';\n216:     let stderr = '';\n217:     let settled = false;\n218:     let timedOut = false;\n219:     let child: ChildProcess;\n220: \n221:     try {\n222:       child = spawn(args.command, args.commandArgs, {\n223:         cwd: args.cwd,\n224:         env: process.env,\n225:         stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n226:       });\n227:     } catch (error: unknown) {\n228:       resolve({\n229:         ok: false,\n230:         stdout,\n231:         stderr: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'spawn failed',\n232:         exitCode: null,\n233:         signal: null,\n234:         errorCode: 'SPAWN_ERROR',\n235:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n236:       });\n237:       return;\n238:     }\n239: \n240:     child.stdin?.write(args.prompt);\n241:     child.stdin?.end();\n242:     const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n243:       timedOut = true;\n244:       child.kill('SIGKILL');\n245:     }, args.timeoutMs);\n246: \n247:     child.stdout?.setEncoding('utf8');\n248:     child.stderr?.setEncoding('utf8');\n249:     child.stdout?.on('data', (chunk: string) => {\n250:       stdout = capOutput(stdout, chunk);\n251:     });\n252:     child.stderr?.on('data', (chunk: string) => {\n253:       stderr = capOutput(stderr, chunk);\n254:     });\n255:     child.on('error', (error: NodeJS.ErrnoException) => {\n256:       if (settled) {\n257:         return;\n258:       }\n259:       settled = true;\n260:       clearTimeout(timer);\n261:       resolve({\n262:         ok: false,\n263:         stdout,\n264:         stderr: error.message,\n265:         exitCode: null,\n266:         signal: null,\n267:         errorCode: error.code === 'ENOENT' ? 'PYTHON_MISSING' : 'SPAWN_ERROR',\n268:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n269:       });\n270:     });\n271:     child.on('close', (exitCode: number | null, signal: NodeJS.Signals | null) => {\n272:       if (settled) {\n273:         return;\n274:       }\n275:       settled = true;\n276:       clearTimeout(timer);\n277:       resolve({\n278:         ok: exitCode === 0 && signal === null && !timedOut,\n279:         stdout,\n280:         stderr,\n281:         exitCode,\n282:         signal,\n283:         errorCode: timedOut || performance.now() - startedAt >= args.timeoutMs\n284:           ? 'TIMEOUT'\n285:           : signal === 'SIGKILL'\n286:             ? 'SIGNAL_KILLED'\n287:             : null,\n288:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n289:       });\n290:     });\n291:   });\n292: }\n293: \n294: async function delay(ms: number): Promise<void> {\n295:   await new Promise((resolve) => {\n296:     setTimeout(resolve, ms);\n297:   });\n298: }\n299: \n300: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n301: // 6. EXPORTS\n302: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n303: \n304: /** Run the Python skill advisor with prompt input carried over stdin. */\n305: export async function runAdvisorSubprocess(\n306:   prompt: string,\n307:   options: AdvisorSubprocessOptions,\n308: ): Promise<AdvisorSubprocessResult> {\n309:   const timeoutMs = options.timeoutMs ?? defaultTimeoutMs();\n310:   const scriptPath = options.scriptPath\n311:     ?? join(\n312:       options.workspaceRoot,\n313:       '.skilled',\n314:       'skills',\n315:       'system-skill-advisor',\n316:       'runtime',\n317:       'scripts',\n318:       'skill_advisor.py',\n319:     );\n320:   const startedAt = performance.now();\n321:   let retriesAttempted = 0;\n322: \n323:   if (!existsSync(scriptPath)) {\n324:     return {\n325:       ok: false,\n326:       recommendations: [],\n327:       errorCode: 'SCRIPT_MISSING',\n328:       exitCode: null,\n329:       signal: null,\n330:       stderr: null,\n331:       durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n332:       retriesAttempted,\n333:     };\n334:   }\n335: \n336:   const commandArgs = [\n337:     scriptPath,\n338:     ...thresholdArgs(options.thresholdConfig),\n339:     '--stdin',\n340:   ];\n341:   const command = options.pythonBin ?? 'python3';\n342: \n343:   for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 2; attempt += 1) {\n344:     const elapsedMs = performance.now() - startedAt;\n345:     const remainingMs = Math.max(0, timeoutMs - elapsedMs);\n346:     const attemptResult = await runSpawnAttempt({\n347:       command,\n348:       commandArgs,\n349:       prompt,\n350:       cwd: options.workspaceRoot,\n351:       timeoutMs: Math.max(1, remainingMs),\n352:     });\n353: \n354:     if (!attemptResult.ok) {\n355:       const busy = SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN.test(attemptResult.stderr);\n356:       const budgetRemaining = timeoutMs - (performance.now() - startedAt);\n357:       if (busy && attempt === 0 && budgetRemaining >= 500) {\n358:         retriesAttempted = 1;\n359:         await delay(options.retryJitterMs?.() ?? 75 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 51));\n360:         continue;\n361:       }\n362:       return {\n363:         ok: false,\n364:         recommendations: [],\n365:         errorCode: busy ? 'SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED' : attemptResult.errorCode ?? 'NON_ZERO_EXIT',\n366:         exitCode: attemptResult.exitCode,\n367:         signal: attemptResult.signal,\n368:         stderr: sanitizeStderr(attemptResult.stderr),\n369:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n370:         retriesAttempted,\n371:       };\n372:     }\n373: \n374:     try {\n375:       return {\n376:         ok: true,\n377:         recommendations: parseRecommendations(attemptResult.stdout),\n378:         errorCode: null,\n379:         exitCode: attemptResult.exitCode,\n380:         signal: attemptResult.signal,\n381:         stderr: sanitizeStderr(attemptResult.stderr),\n382:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n383:         retriesAttempted,\n384:       };\n385:     } catch (error: unknown) {\n386:       return {\n387:         ok: false,\n388:         recommendations: [],\n389:         errorCode: error instanceof SyntaxError ? 'JSON_PARSE_FAILED' : 'INVALID_JSON_SHAPE',\n390:         exitCode: attemptResult.exitCode,\n391:         signal: attemptResult.signal,\n392:         stderr: null,\n393:         durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n394:         retriesAttempted,\n395:       };\n396:     }\n397:   }\n398: \n399:   return {\n400:     ok: false,\n401:     recommendations: [],\n402:     errorCode: 'SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED',\n403:     exitCode: null,\n404:     signal: null,\n405:     stderr: null,\n406:     durationMs: performance.now() - startedAt,\n407:     retriesAttempted,\n408:   };\n409: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589259896,"end":1794589260374}}}}
