{"type":"text","timestamp":1794589441267,"sessionID":"ses_e2a2563b3ffeIDE7F73WqgBQI8","part":{"id":"prt_1d5dd7d3f0024UVMWw79AoYxEl","sessionID":"ses_e2a2563b3ffeIDE7F73WqgBQI8","messageID":"msg_1d5dd640d0011EIEMb862Uc771","type":"text","text":"Files written:\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` — renamed the cap case to `retries once on a busy marker written after the cap` (expects `SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED`, `retriesAttempted` 1), replaced the comment above it, and added the split-write case.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts` — added `sawBusy` to `SpawnAttemptResult`, a `busyCarry`/`sawBusy` scan in the stderr `data` handler ahead of `capOutput`, `sawBusy` on all three `resolve` calls, and the retry decision now reads `attemptResult.sawBusy || SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN.test(attemptResult.stderr)`.\n\nVerify output:\n\nTest-first run, both new cases failed as named:\n```\nFAIL tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts > runAdvisorSubprocess output cap > retries once on a busy marker written after the cap\nAssertionError: expected 'NON_ZERO_EXIT' to be 'SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED'\nFAIL tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts > runAdvisorSubprocess output cap > retries once on a busy marker split across two writes after the cap\nAssertionError: expected 'NON_ZERO_EXIT' to be 'SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED'\nTests  2 failed | 1 passed (3)\n```\n\nAfter the change:\n```\nVX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts  → Test Files 1 passed (1), Tests 3 passed (3)\nVX tests/legacy/advisor-subprocess.vitest.ts → Test Files 1 passed (1), Tests 9 passed (9)\nTC (npm run typecheck) → EXIT=0\nnode TSX $PL/probe-busy-cap.mts →\n  marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1\n  marker first: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1\n```\n\n`git status --porcelain` on the two named files shows only those two as modified. T029 is left unticked. Nothing was blocked.\n\nSKILL ROUTING: User directed → sk-code (artifact trigger, code edit). ARTIFACT: sk-code → TypeScript implementation and verification. REPO RULES: prevent-overengineering.md, scope-discipline.md, evidence-and-proof.md, communication.md, communication-handoff.md.","time":{"start":1794589424959,"end":1794589441267}}}
